    "name": "Bok choi raab-",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Bok choy raab</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> (also called bok choy rabe) isthe tender, flowering stalk that appears when overwintered or mature bok choy bolts in the spring. It features sweet, crunchy stalks, delicate leafy greens, and edible yellow buds. Its flavor is a delicious cross between traditional bok choy and broccoli rabe, with a slightly mustardy kick.</span></p>",
